{
 "dur": 73.4,
 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "v01",
   "t": 0.4,
   "chunks": [
    "What's actually inside",
    "a military recon drone?",
    "Let's take one apart."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02",
   "t": 5.4,
   "chunks": [
    "Small recon drones are often",
    "hand-launched planes:",
    "under two kilos,",
    "with a wingspan around 1.5 meters."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03",
   "t": 13.22,
   "chunks": [
    "An electric motor",
    "spins the propeller.",
    "A rechargeable battery fills the fuselage,",
    "good for an hour or more aloft."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v04",
   "t": 21.06,
   "chunks": [
    "The brain is",
    "the flight controller.",
    "Gyros and accelerometers feel every tilt,",
    "and GPS tells it where it is."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v05",
   "t": 28.7,
   "chunks": [
    "Autopilot software flies",
    "a preplanned route of waypoints",
    "on its own,",
    "or a pilot takes over by hand."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v06",
   "t": 35.48,
   "chunks": [
    "A radio datalink",
    "streams live video to a ground station,",
    "out to around ten kilometers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v07",
   "t": 41.31,
   "chunks": [
    "And under the nose, the whole point:",
    "a stabilized camera turret,",
    "with a daylight and a thermal camera."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v08",
   "t": 48.75,
   "chunks": [
    "So where does Palantir fit in?",
    "It doesn't build the drone.",
    "It builds the software."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v09",
   "t": 53.75,
   "chunks": [
    "The Pentagon's Maven system,",
    "largely built on Palantir software,",
    "fuses drone video with other feeds,",
    "flags objects with computer vision,",
    "and maps them for human analysts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v10",
   "t": 66.36,
   "chunks": [
    "What should we take apart next?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v11",
   "t": 68.57,
   "chunks": [
    "Congrats! You've discovered",
    "the recon drone."
   ]
  }
 ]
}